  <div class="container listing-page">
  <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">/ THE NOTEBOOK</p><h1>About BinRev<span class="brand-dot">.</span></h1><p>A place to document what happens behind the binary.</p></header>
  <div class="about-content prose"><h2>Read. Reverse. Document.</h2><p>BinRev collects malware analysis and reverse-engineering notes. The focus is on following execution, understanding unpacking and injection techniques, and extracting the details that explain a sample’s behavior.</p><p>The analyses are working research notes. They capture the process alongside the findings: the dead ends, the useful breakpoints, and the pieces that eventually fit together.</p><h2>A reference for the reversing desk</h2><p>The resource library brings together visual workflows, low-level Windows structures, and the Portable Executable format. Diagrams are available as SVGs, and the Excalidraw originals are available for editing.</p><h2>Follow the source</h2><p>The site and its notes live in <a href="https://github.com/LarsAndre/BinRev">LarsAndre/BinRev on GitHub</a>.</p></div>
